{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $(1,10)$ such that $g'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $g$ over the interval:\n\n$g'(c)=\\dfrac{g(10)-g(1)}{(10)-(1)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{g(10)-g(1)}{(10)-(1)}=\\dfrac{7-2}{9}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{5}{9}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $g$ and find the $x$-value for which $g'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{5}{9}}$.\n\n$g'(x)=\\dfrac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-1}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $g'(x)=\\dfrac{5}{9}$ is $x=4.25$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=4.25$ is indeed within the interval $(1,10)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{5x-1}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(5x-1)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(5x-1)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(5x-1)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{5x-1}}(5)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-1}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-1}}\u0026=\\dfrac{5}{9}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{5x-1}\u0026=\\dfrac{9}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{5x-1})^2\u0026=\\left(\\dfrac{9}{2}\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n5x-1\u0026=\\dfrac{81}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\n5x\u0026=\\dfrac{85}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=4.25\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=4.25$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=\\sqrt{5x-1}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $g$ on the interval $[1,10]$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$2.25$","correct":false},{"content":"$4.25$","correct":true},{"content":"$6.5$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$8$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
